Dear Miguel,

I do not know what the problem is, but I would suggest trying to run 
RSiena without any other packages and in a clean workspace i.e. start R 
in a directory with no stored .RData, load only RSiena and run the 
script example.

If the problem only happens with sub processes, is it possible that the 
subprocesses are using a different version of R or RSiena? Or getting a 
different workspace initially? Will all these packages be loaded in each 
sub process?

There has been a major change in the parallel processing in RSiena in R 
2.14.0, although the code is designed to still run under R-2.13.n. The 
new version should be more efficient on Linux than the old one. Thus it 
might be a good idea to upgrade the R if you can.

Regards,

Ruth

